            0.584,
            0.027,
            0.804,
            0.043
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 5 — Exploring Forces"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.893,
            0.03,
            0.917,
            0.045
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "65"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.084,
            0.745,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In everyday life, we come across many situations where a force is applied (Fig. 5.2), for example, opening a drawer, stretching a rubber band, a fielder stopping a ball, kicking a football, applying brakes on a moving bicycle, rolling a chapati, or turning the steering handle of an autorickshaw. What effect can the application of force have on objects?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.203,
            0.464,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The force applied on an object may"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.226,
            0.468,
            0.244
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z make an object move from rest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.249,
            0.59,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z change the speed of an object if it is moving."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.273,
            0.584,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "change the direction of motion of an object."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.297,
            0.613,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z bring about a change in the shape of an object."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.34,
            0.249,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.134,
                0.34,
                0.249,
                0.45
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.351,
            0.508,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does this mean that whenever there is a change in speed or direction, or change in shape, a force is a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "cting on the object?",
              "styles": [
                "underline"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.545,
            0.368,
            0.763,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Yes, none of these take place without the action of force."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.774,
            0.306,
            0.912,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.774,
                0.306,
                0.912,
                0.439
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.467,
            0.309,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A step further"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.5,
            0.735,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose an object is at rest. Does it mean that no force is acting on this object? It means that the forces acting on the object are balancing one another. You will learn about balanced forces in higher grades."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.74,
            0.444,
            0.906,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.74,
                0.444,
                0.906,
                0.573
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.59,
            0.485,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z cause some or all of these effects."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.638,
            0.692,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.3 Are Forces an Interaction Between Two or More Objects?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.704,
            0.743,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When you push a table, your hand is one object applying force on another object — the table. Here, we say that your hand and the table are two objects interacting with each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.762,
            0.744,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think of all the actions listed in Table 5.1. How many objects are involved in each of the actions? Do you "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "notice",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that forces result only when two objects are interacting in some way or the other? From these examples, we can "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "infer",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that at least two objects must interact for a force to come into play."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.857,
            0.744,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "force",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a push or pull on an object resulting from the object’s interaction with another object. The "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SI unit of force is newton",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (written with a small ‘n’) and its "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "symbol is N",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
